From: Nick DiZazzo <nick.dizazzo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:37:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] fix(skippy): take the argmax path for temperature-0
 chains that can only pick the top logit

skippy_sampling_is_greedy_equivalent rejects temperature-0 requests
that set ignore_eos, carry a logit bias, or set penalties with a zero
window. Those requests build the full default chain and, for every row,
copy all logits into a candidate array and run penalties, DRY,
top-n-sigma, top-k, top-p, min-p, XTC, temperature and dist on the
scheduler thread, although the chain can only return the top biased
logit.

The chat sampling path now checks once per chain whether every
configured sampler keeps the top logit (temperature 0, no dynamic
temperature or mirostat, and penalties, DRY, typical-p and XTC
disabled). It then scans the raw logits plus the chain's biases for a
unique finite maximum. A tie, NaN or non-finite maximum falls back to
the full chain, so the selected token is the one the chain would
select. The chain still accepts every token, so penalty history stays
in step. Grammar and reasoning-budget samplers keep the full path.

The new logic lives in sampling_argmax.cpp, because sampling.cpp is
over 1,000 lines. No public header or ABI changes.
